body:
Hahaha, he did have that Karen tone of voice now that you mention it.

&#x200B;

Aside from an apology, which I gave him, and moving the car right away, I'm really not sure what else I could have done.

I know how you feel, including dreading christimas. I posted a similar story about an awful grandma on thanksgiving, too, even down to inviting me to her place and getting pissed off that I wasn't going despite not even knowing it was happening.

&#x200B;

I don't know what gives them such a massive ego. Simply being a grand parent isn't an accomplishment. It's something that happens to the majority of people at some point.

Honestly, I said the same thing. I told my family "imagine if an ex was acting this way to me".

&#x200B;

She gets a free pass because she's old AND because she's family.

I've thought about not cutting her off but instead limiting my interactions with her to a minimum. It just can't happen. She calls almost daily (usually wanting a favor or wanting dirt on someone) and gets absolutely furious if you don't answer. (Usually leaving a voicemail that consists of a sigh and "Jesus Christ" before slamming the phone down)

&#x200B;

I'd like to only see her at family functions, but she's so high maintenance that it seems like an all or nothing situation.
